            "review_title": "Review at Banh Canh Cua 102",
            "review_text": "Michelle Yip\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia178 contributions\n0\nHidden gem!\nMar 2018 • Couples\nThis place is situated opposite the Danang train station, with a huge orange sign board, it would be hard to miss. Don't be fooled by its quiet interior and lack of crowd. We decided to give this a try because they were using fresh ingredients in their dishes. This place is also tourist-friendly as the menu has an English option, AND, they charge the same price to locals and tourists alike. Price wise, it is extremely reasonable. Taste wise, it was really flavourful. It was so good we went back to this shop twice. The noodle was a springy rice-noodle that complemented the soup, which wasn't spicy (by Malaysian standard). You can choose to mix your noodle with a combination of ingredients such as prawns, crab meat, crab cakes, pork balls, chicken. The sides are also worth ordering as well, especially the fried pastry. Goes really well when you dunk it into the soup. For those who are in this part of town, you need to have a meal at this place. Guaranteed to keep you full and satisfied.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 11, 2018",
